<title>MEXICO: Pemex says two crude ports shut due to bad weather.</title>
<headline>Pemex says two crude ports shut due to bad weather.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petroleos Mexicanos said two crude oil shipping ports were closed at 7 a.m. (1300 GMT) because of high winds.</p>
<p>The state-owned oil and gas company said Dos Bocas in Tabasco state and Pajaritos in Veracruz state along the Gulf of Mexico were shut. The two terminals are among Pemex's three main crude exporting sites.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7903</p>
</text>
